WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.940
Following in the footsteps of names like the late&nbsp;
Christopher Reeve and Brandon Routh, Henry Cavill&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:11.100
debuted as Superman in 2013. Starring in the&nbsp;
DC Extended Universe-launching "Man of Steel,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:16.860
this take on Kal-El was quite different from his&nbsp;
predecessors. His more thoughtful, somber Superman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:22.680
occupied a dark, moody world, but that didn't&nbsp;
turn all DC fans away. Many came to love Cavill's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:27.420
approach to the character, which is why he&nbsp;
continued to appear in the DCEU in future films.

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:31.980
In the wake of "Batman v. Superman: Dawn of&nbsp;
Justice" and both cuts of "Justice League,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:36.600
Cavill's version of Superman wound up in&nbsp;
limbo. Fans couldn't help but wonder if his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:41.640
run was over as the DCEU struggled to find&nbsp;
its footing. Then came 2022's "Black Adam,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:46.260
where Cavill got one more crack at the part in a&nbsp;
post-credits sequence. One would have to imagine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:51.000
that this was a sign he was back for the long&nbsp;
haul. However, as we learned on December 14,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:56.160
2022, this won't be the case as a new&nbsp;
Superman-centric film is developed.

00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:00.240
There's certainly an argument to be made&nbsp;
that Henry Cavill never got his proper due&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:05.640
as Superman and should continue as the legendary&nbsp;
DC hero on the silver screen. However, it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:11.160
important to face the facts: recasting Superman&nbsp;
is the best way to go at this stage in the game.

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:16.620
In October 2022, James Gunn and Peter&nbsp;
Safran were announced as the leaders of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:21.180
a new division of Warner Bros. Discovery&nbsp;
called DC Studios. The goal of this group&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:26.340
is to ensure continuity and consistent&nbsp;
quality across most DC Comics-based films,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:31.140
and television projects. If Gunn and&nbsp;
Safran want to keep the DCU in order,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:36.480
they must come to accept the fact that with&nbsp;
continuity issues, retcons, and more, it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:41.220
past the point of fixing. Therefore, scrapping&nbsp;
everything and starting fresh is their best move.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:47.400
This means letting Henry Cavill go in favor of&nbsp;
a new Superman actor. After all, Superman isn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:52.320
just some minor player. He's Superman. If they&nbsp;
really want to convince fans they're entering a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:56.580
new-and-improved era of DC media, it would be&nbsp;
counterproductive to bring back the previous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.580 --> 00:02:02.220
version of their tentpole character to lead the&nbsp;
charge. Besides, it also puts an end to this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:07.200
strange and frustrating limbo Henry Cavill's&nbsp;
Superman has been trapped in for years now.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:11.400
Even though it's best for him to leave&nbsp;
the role behind, there's no denying how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:15.960
much Henry Cavill loves Superman. He went&nbsp;
above and beyond to be the best version&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:19.860
of "The Man of Steel" that he could,&nbsp;
and if the DCU wasn't in the process&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:25.320
of a soft reboot, he could easily remain.&nbsp;
Unfortunately, due to no fault of his own,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:30.600
Cavill's portrayal just has too much baggage&nbsp;
for him to carry on under Gunn and Safran.

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:35.400
"Now the cameras are waiting at your ship, for&nbsp;
the world to see the holes in the holy. Yes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:37.980
the almighty comes clean about&nbsp;
how dirty he is when it counts."

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:43.380
Most of the films he's appeared in have proven&nbsp;
critically divisive, namely "Batman v. Superman:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:47.220
Dawn of Justice." Many also stem&nbsp;
from the now-defunct Snyderverse:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:52.500
a string of DCEU entries tied to director&nbsp;
Zack Snyder that, according to Collider,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.580
Warner Bros. Discovery has tried to&nbsp;
distance itself from in recent years.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.580 --> 00:03:02.040
The "Justice League" CGI upper lip debacle and&nbsp;
dead-end "Black Adam" cameo didn't help either.

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:07.200
So is Henry Cavill destined to never play&nbsp;
Superman again? Maybe, but as comic book&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:12.240
media has proven over the years, it's smart&nbsp;
to never say never. From Michael Keaton as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:17.700
Batman to Hugh Jackman as Wolverine, legacy&nbsp;
actors returning to their superhero roles is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:22.740
far from uncommon. Once enough time passes,&nbsp;
the DCU finds its groove with a new Superman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:26.460
and a narrative opportunity arises,&nbsp;
perhaps Cavill could return to play&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.460 --> 00:03:31.620
the same version of the beloved hero we've come&nbsp;
to recognize — or one from another timeline.

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:35.700
Then again, with Cavill no longer&nbsp;
playing the main DCU Superman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:39.180
that does free him up to take on&nbsp;
another role in the canon. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:43.260
the same day his Superman departure was&nbsp;
announced, James Gunn mentioned on Twitter:

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:48.000
"We just had a great meeting with Henry&nbsp;
and we're big fans and we talked about a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:50.820
number of exciting possibilities&nbsp;
to work together in the future."

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:52.980
"I have so many questions."

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:57.360
Could he be a member of the Green Lantern&nbsp;
Corps? Bizarro? Bat-Mite? Time will tell,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.360 --> 00:04:01.980
but hopefully, he'll get to sink his&nbsp;
teeth into a new DC role down the line.

